1
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
A priceless true story.

2
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:46,000
The Duke is a comedy, drama, history film directed by Roger Michell.

3
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
In 1961, a 60-year-old taxi driver stole Goya’s portrait of the Duke
of Wellington from the National Gallery in London.

4
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:26,000
It was the first (and remains the only) theft in the Gallery’s history.

5
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
What happened next became the stuff of legend.

6
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Kempton Bunton, played by Jim Broadbent.

7
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Dorothy Bunton, played by Helen Mirren.

8
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Jackie Bunton, played by Fionn Whitehead.

9
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Mrs. Gowling, played by Anna Maxwell Martin.

10
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Jeremy Hutchinson, played by Matthew Goode.

11
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Kenny Bunton, played by Jack Bandeira.

12
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
The Duke is a 2020 British comedy drama film directed by Roger Michell,
with a screenplay by Richard Bean and Clive Coleman.

13
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
It is based on the true story of the 1961 theft of the Portrait
of the Duke of Wellington by Kempton Bunton.

14
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
The film stars Jim Broadbent, Helen Mirren, Fionn
Whitehead, Anna Maxwell Martin, and Matthew Goode.

15
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
It was Michell's penultimate film before his death on 22 September 2021.

16
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:26,000
The film was released in cinemas in the UK on 25
February 2022 to generally good reviews.

17
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
